  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {欠|か}ける (intransitive — to be lacking, to be missing)\n\nUSAGE:\nAlmost exclusively used in the negative: {欠|か}かさない (to never miss) or {欠|か}かさず (without fail). The affirmative form is rare.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{欠|か}かさない: to never miss 〜\n- {欠|か}かさず〜する: to do 〜 without fail\n- {一日|いちにち}も{欠|か}かさず: without missing a single day\n- {欠|か}かすことのできない: indispensable, essential\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{欠|か}かしている is uncommon. The habitual negative {欠|か}かさない is the standard form.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {欠|か}ける: to be lacking, to be missing (intransitive)\n- {欠|けっ}{席|せき}する: to be absent",
